    "Notes Updated": "5/20/2026",
    "Scouting Notes": "Starter\n Seems to be getting more out of his lower half early this year, a bit more explosive with the movement now\n Fastball shape has taken a step forward this season, as well as the velo (likely tied to the more explosive movement). He's now getting up to 98 MPH, sitting around 95.\n Slider has sharpened up a bit too, sitting in the 83-85 MPH range, with some late drop to it and a bit of glove-side movement as well\n Curveball is thrown a bit slower, with a bit more movement vertically and horizontally\n Sinker shape still not my favorite, but gets a lot of arm-side run which helps it play up with the four-seam improvements\n Still really like the way he sells the changeup and the way it fades for him\n Command has looked really strong early in 2026 as well.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/2/2024",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Extremely projectable arm\n Some similarities to Bishop Letson in terms of lankiness and extension potential\n Two fastballs, have both flashed pretty interesting characteristics in terms of ride vs run\n Slider is s sweeper-ish in terms of the plane it's on, could be an above average offering\n Changeup is a definite WIP, but shows signs of good fade and velo differential",
